
###ZTAA: Desktop Watermark & Endpoint Policy Configuration Guide
To enhance data security and discourage unauthorized screen capture or screen recording, ZTAA offers a Watermark Endpoint Policy that displays a non-removable watermark on the user's screen once a VPN connection is established. The watermark disappears automatically when the VPN disconnects.

###Acceptance Criteria
 The watermark must appear automatically when VPN is connected
  The watermark must be removed once VPN is disconnected
  The user must not be able to tamper with, remove, or bypass the watermark
###Supported Operating Systems
Windows


macOS


Linux


Android


iOS


###Section 1: Configuring Desktop Watermark
### Prerequisite
Admin access to the ZTAA (InstaSafe) Console


### Steps to Configure Desktop Watermark Settings
Go to Perimeter Management > Desktop Watermark


Click on (+) Add New Desktop Watermark


Enter a Display Name and click Submit


Click on the newly created Desktop Watermark profile


Click Upload to add the Watermark Logo


Optionally, enter your Company Slogan


Enable any of the following display fields as per your preference:


Username


Tenant Slug


Client IP


Date


Device ID


Adjust the opacity level of the watermark



###Section 2: Configuring the Watermark Endpoint Policy
### Steps to Configure Watermark Endpoint Policy
Log in to the InstaSafe Console with Admin credentials


Go to Access Policy > Endpoint Policy


Click Add Policy


Enter a Display Name for the policy


Click Next


Select Watermark and proceed


Choose the previously configured Desktop Watermark profile


Select the Operating System(s) to apply the policy to


Click Next


Add the target User(s) or User Group(s)


Set the condition to "When VPN is Connected"


Click Next and then Submit



Section 3: Testing Watermark via ZTNA UI Client
### Prerequisites
The user must be assigned to a VPN application


The ZTNA UI Client must be installed


### Steps to Verify Watermark Display
Launch the ZTNA UI Client


Enter the InstaSafe Workspace URL


Authenticate via the redirected InstaSafe login page


When prompted, click "Open InstaSafe ZTNA Agent"


The ZTNA Agent will launch — click Connect


Upon connection, the watermark will appear on the desktop screen


 






